course: dictionary
lesson: 10351
title: Transparent: clear and open
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Transparent means you can see clearly through something, like clear glass or clean water. «Transparent materials let light through, translucent ones let some through, and opaque ones block it.» Transparent is the clearest of the three: almost all the light gets through.
explain: The word also describes people and choices. «Being transparent means your decisions can be seen and checked: what you noticed and which rule you used.» A transparent decision is open and honest, with nothing hidden, so you can see how and why it was made.
explain: Use the context to check. In «a transparent excuse», the excuse is easy to see through, so nobody believes it. Try your meaning in the sentence: "an easy-to-see-through excuse" still makes sense, so transparent fits.
fact: Transparent means clear enough to see through.
fact: «Transparent» materials, like clear glass and clean water, let almost all light through.
fact: Translucent lets some light through, like frosted glass; opaque blocks it, like wood.
fact: «Transparent» can also mean honest and open, with nothing hidden.
fact: Phrases to know: transparent plastic, a transparent excuse (one that is easy to see through).
exercise: «Glass is transparent.» What does transparent mean here? | Very loud | Made of wood | Dark and heavy | *Clear, so you can see through it
exercise: Which material lets almost all the light through? | Frosted glass | *Clean water | Wood | Brick
exercise: «A transparent decision» means what? | *Open, so you can see how and why it was made | Hidden in a box | Quick and easy | Made of glass
test: «He gave a transparent excuse, and nobody believed him.» What does transparent suggest? | Hidden under a rock | Very long and detailed | Clear glass in a window | *Easy to see through, so it is not believed
test: Which word means that some light gets through? | *Translucent | Transparent | Opaque | Glowing
exam: Tom says transparent only means clear glass. Is he right? | No, it means very loud | *No, it can also mean honest, with nothing hidden | Yes, glass is the only thing it describes | Yes, and only in science lessons
